  "limitations": [
    "This is a native arithmetic trial, not an implemented production optimization or a cold packaging speedup. Fixed hosted tool binaries still use the previous implementation. Rebuilding and promoting them remains separate work.",
    "The candidate replaces two-input modular addition with low-31-bit addition XOR the two high bits. The low sum is at most 2^32-2. Four/five-input sums accumulate all low and high 16-bit halves directly: Low is at most 262140/327675; High including carry is at most 262143/327679. All intermediate checked additions remain within u32.",
    "Known-answer inputs are repeated byte 97 with lengths 0,1,55,56,63,64,65,4097,65536,1048576 and digest constants generated by Node crypto. Range updates use chunks of at most 4097 bytes. Randomized input, direct arithmetic edge cases, malformed streaming states, and full 64 MiB limits are not exhaustively qualified by this trial.",
    "Windows observed kernel peak working sets were 7270400-7274496 bytes before and 7278592-7720960 after. Debian observed VmHWM values were 1683456-1687552 before and 1695744 after. Values sampled every 20 ms may omit the final interval and are not cross-host comparable or strict peak bounds.",
    "Candidate WVB size rises from 29815 to 30731 bytes. Windows application size rises from 567808 to 578560 bytes; Linux from 569344 to 577536 bytes. Timing gains trade a small code-size increase for fewer executed helper calls.",
    "Three alternating samples per variant establish a useful local signal but no enforced performance threshold. Full compiler and qualification benchmarks were not rerun.",
    "Changed-file routing selects only seed for Foundation/Sha256-Compression.wv. Inspection found eight source projects in the pinned seed plan, each with one source reference, and none uses the compression or streaming source. An existing appropriate owner must acquire direct streaming-hash coverage before production promotion; routing alone is not passing evidence.",
    "Initial fixture data names ending with a numeric word were rejected by bytecode semantic admission. Corrected word names passed the unchanged verifier. Those failed diagnostic attempts are not successful build evidence.",
    "Raw sources, executables, results and summary under Artifacts are ignored local diagnostics, identified by hashes here rather than distributed in Git."
  ],
